{{!-- Every writer on a post, as plain text.

	{{> "byline"}}      called in a post's context

A post has an ordered list of authors and Ghost's own {{authors}} helper renders it — but that
helper's autolink either wraps every name in an unclassed `<a>` or drops the link entirely, and
this theme's bylines are drawn either as unlinked meta text or as links carrying a class. So the
list is walked here instead, once, and byline-links.hbs is the linked half of the same drawing.

`{{#primary_author}}{{name}}{{/primary_author}}` is what these bylines used to say, and on a
co-authored post that silently credits one of the writers. `primary_author` still supplies the
FACE — the design draws one — but the credit names everyone.

The separators are content, not decoration, so neither is aria-hidden: a screen reader reading
"Marisol Ade and Erin Laurier" is reading what the page says. The middot between the byline and
the date is decorative and stays hidden at its own call site. --}}
{{~#foreach authors~}}
	{{~#unless @first}}{{#if @last}}{{t " and "}}{{else}}, {{/if}}{{/unless~}}
	{{~name~}}
{{~/foreach~}}
